C.4 Quotation Status Machine (Defined)
draft
  ↓ (Pricing submits for review)
internal_review
  ↓ (Approved internally)
sent_to_sales
  ↓ (Salesperson sends to customer)
customer_discussion
  ├─→ revision_requested ──→ [NEW VERSION] ──→ draft
  └─→ customer_approved ──→ [FREEZE] ──→ KYC → Job
  ├─→ rejected
  ├─→ expired
  └─→ cancelled
Legal Transitions Only:
draft → internal_review | cancelled
internal_review → sent_to_sales | draft | cancelled
sent_to_sales → customer_discussion | internal_review | cancelled
customer_discussion → revision_requested | customer_approved | rejected | expired
revision_requested → draft (NEW VERSION)
customer_approved → Terminal - triggers KYC
rejected, expired, cancelled → Terminal
C.5 Versioning Strategy: parent_quotation_id + version
-- Version 1 (original)
INSERT INTO quotations (enquiry_id, version, ...) 
VALUES (enq_id, 1, ...);

-- Revision requested → NEW ROW
INSERT INTO quotations (enquiry_id, parent_quotation_id, version, ...)
VALUES (enq_id, v1_id, 2, ...);

-- Query latest: WHERE enquiry_id = ? ORDER BY version DESC LIMIT 1
-- History: SELECT * FROM quotations WHERE enquiry_id = ? ORDER BY version
Why not quotation_group_id? Self-ref is simpler, enforces linear history, and parent_quotation_id makes revision chain explicit.
C.6 Pricing Calculation Model (Per-Line Cost + Sell)
Field	Source	Notes
cost_rate	Manual entry / Vendor quote	Required
cost_currency	Manual	Default INR
cost_exchange_rate	Manual / Exchange rate table	Snapshotted
cost_amount	cost_rate * qty * cost_exch_rate	GENERATED
margin_pct	Per-line override OR quotation default	Per-line hybrid
selling_rate	cost_rate * (1 + margin/100)	GENERATED
selling_currency	Manual	Usually quote_currency
selling_amount	selling_rate * qty	GENERATED
Margin Model: Hybrid (Global default + Per-line override)
quotations.margin_pct = global default
quotation_items.margin_pct = NULL (use global) OR override value
C.7 Multi-Currency Model
Aspect	Decision
Base Currency	INR (system default)
Quote Currency	Per quotation (INR/USD/EUR/GBP)
Cost Currency	Per line item (vendor may quote in USD)
Exchange Rate	Snapshotted on Quotation (exchange_rate, exchange_rate_date, source)
Cost Conversion	cost_amount = cost_rate * qty * cost_exchange_rate
Sell Conversion	selling_amount = selling_rate * qty (in quote_currency)
Critical: All rates snapshotted on quotation creation. Historical quotations never change.
C.8 Vendor Architecture
Vendor Master (vendors)
      │
      ├──< Vendor Quotes (vendor_quotes) ──< Quotation Version
      │
      └──< Quotation Items (vendor_id FK, optional)
Vendor is a master (reusable, GST/PAN validated like Customer)
vendor_quotes = formal vendor submissions attached to a quotation version
quotation_items.vendor_id = which vendor's cost rate used for this line
